{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_9",
      "quote": "(1) Study design: All included studies were RCTs; (2) Participants: All patients aged \u2265 18 years diagnosed with heart failure who meeting the diagnostic criteria and classified as NYHA functional class II-IV (NYHA classification was based on the 2022 AHA/ACC/HFSA Heart Failure Guideline, defining classes I-IV as: Class I, no limitation; Class II, slight limitation with ordinary activity; Class III, marked limitation with less-than-ordinary activity; Class IV, symptoms at rest.); (3) Interventions: The experimental group received conventional Western medicine (including diuretics, angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors [ACEIs] or angiotensin receptor blockers [ARBs], digitalis preparations, \u03b2-blockers, aldosterone receptor antagonists, nitrates, etc.) in accordance with contemporary heart failure treatment guidelines [1], supplemented with plant extracts. The control group received only conventional Western medicine; (4) Outcome measures: At least one of the following was assessed: Number of patients with improved NYHA classification, LVEF, 6MWT, or QoL.",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies key study characteristics used for eligibility (study design, participant age and NYHA class, interventions, and outcomes) but does not report setting details or any follow-up/timeframe requirements, so the element is only partially satisfied."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "A comprehensive search was conducted across four electronic databases (PubMed, EMBASE, the Cochrane Library, and Web of Science) from their inception to June 2024. ... The detailed search strategy is provided in Supplementary Table S1, S2, S3, and S4. It should be noted that this search was restricted to published literature. Therefore, citation tracking was not performed, and clinical trial registries such as ClinicalTrials.gov or the Chinese Clinical Trial Registry (ChiCTR) were not searched.",
      "reason": "The review states a publication-status restriction (published literature only) and gives the date range of the search (inception to June 2024), but it does not specify language restrictions or other report characteristics (e.g., dissemination years beyond the search end date or gray literature policies), so this element is partially met."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The provided evidence lists general exclusion reasons (e.g., incomplete data, not meeting outcomes) but does not explicitly distinguish excluding studies because outcomes were not measured from excluding studies because outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_16",
      "quote": "A total of 28 RCTs involving 3,650 patients with heart failure were included. ... Fifteen herbal extracts were compared, including Astragalus extract (6 studies) ... The primary outcomes assessed included Number of patients with improved NYHA classification, LVEF, 6MWT, or QoL. ... Twenty studies involving 13 interventions were included for Number of patients with improved NYHA classification, with the network evidence diagram presented in Fig. 2A.",
      "reason": "The review specifies the intervention groups (multiple named plant-extract interventions and conventional treatment control), links them to the outcomes, and identifies which interventions were included in the network syntheses, thereby specifying groups used in each synthesis and linking them to the review comparisons."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "Although the manuscript notes a restriction to published literature and that registries/citation tracking were not searched, it does not provide a rationale explaining why these notable restrictions on eligibility were applied."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "75"
}

